    "description": "• Designed and developed a company wide website used by program management to perform project planning and resource allocation analysis. The website uses Java, SQL, jQuery, HighCharts, JSP, Tomcat and PostgreSQL for dynamic creation of graphical charts and tables. As the only team member, performed all phases of SDLC including: requirements gathering, UML model, ER Diagrams, coding, configuration management, server installation, deployment and training. Resulted in an increase of staffing reporting accuracy by 33%  \n• Developed a web service application using Apache Axis, to collect data from various information providers and to disseminate that data via push notifications to subscribed clients in real-time.   The tactical information web service was adopted as a common platform that led to securing additional contracts with the U.S. Navy and the Marines\n• Performed trade study on using a product line approach for developing software. Resulted in a contract with the US Navy to refactor their existing software design to a component based architecture using open standards\n• Established a ClearCase multisite development infrastructure between Northrop Grumman and US Navy. The automatic repository synchronizations increase productivity between the two sites\n• Trained US Navy on using ClearCase Unified Change Management (UCM)\n• Created an automatic build system using Ant for rapid deployment of component based products\n• Two time TAP (Timely Awards Plan) winner for outstanding accomplishments on the development of the tactical information web service\n• Promoted within 3 years of hire to level 5 Engineer (out of 6 levels)",
